|-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\|/-\| Here’s a C++ function that converts Markdown-formatted text to HTML. This implementation handles basic Markdown syntax (bold, italics, links, headings, lists, and horizontal rules) and converts it to corresponding HTML tags:

```cpp
#include <string>
#include <algorithm>

std::string markdownToHtml(const std::string& markdown) {
    std::string html;
    size_t pos = 0;

    while (pos < markdown.size()) {
        // Handle headings (e.g., # Heading)
        if (pos + 1 < markdown.size() && markdown[pos] == '#') {
            size_t end = markdown.find('\n', pos);
            std::string heading = markdown.substr(pos, end - pos);
            int level = 0;
            for (char c : heading) {
                if (c == '#') level++;
                else break;
            }
            html += "<h" + std::to_string(level) + ">" + heading.substr(level) + "</h" + std::to_string(level) + ">";
            pos = end;
            continue;
        }

        // Handle bold (**bold**)
        else if (pos + 1 < markdown.size() && markdown[pos] == '*') {
            size_t start = pos;
            pos++;
            while (pos < markdown.size() && markdown[pos] != '*') pos++;
            if (pos < markdown.size()) {
                html += "<strong>" + markdown.substr(start, pos - start) + "</strong>";
                pos++;
            }
            continue;
        }

        // Handle italic (*italic*)
        else if (pos + 1 < markdown.size() && markdown[pos] == '*') {
            size_t start = pos;
            pos++;
            while (pos < markdown.size() && markdown[pos] != '*') pos++;
            if (pos < markdown.size()) {
                html += "<em>" + markdown.substr(start, pos - start) + "</em>";
                pos++;
            }
            continue;
        }

        // Handle links ([text](url))
        else if (pos + 1 < markdown.size() && markdown[pos] == '[') {
            size_t start = pos;
            pos++;
            size_t end = markdown.find(']', pos);
            if (end == std::string::npos) break;

            // Extract link text
            size_t text_start = pos;
            while (pos < end && markdown[pos] != '(') pos++;
            std::string text = markdown.substr(text_start, pos - text_start);

            // Extract URL
            pos++;
            size_t url_start = pos;
            while (pos < markdown.size() && markdown[pos] != ')') pos++;
            std::string url = markdown.substr(url_start, pos - url_start);

            html += "<a href=\"" + url + "\">" + text + "</a>";
            pos = end + 1;
            continue;
        }

        // Handle lists (bullet points)
        else if (pos < markdown.size() && markdown[pos] == '-') {
            html += "<li>";
            pos++;
            // Skip to next line or end of list item
            while (pos < markdown.size() && markdown[pos] != '\n') pos++;
            html += "</li>";
            continue;
        }

        // Handle horizontal rule (---)
        else if (pos + 2 < markdown.size() && markdown.substr(pos, 3) == "---") {
            html += "<hr>";
            pos += 3;
            continue;
        }

        // Default: copy as-is (no conversion)
        html += markdown.substr(pos, 1);
        pos++;
    }

    return html;
}
```

### Notes:
1. **Limitations**: This is a basic implementation. For a production system, you'd need to handle more Markdown features (e.g., code blocks, tables, images, nested lists, etc.).
2. **Edge Cases**: The function skips unhandled Markdown syntax (e.g., `**bold**` is converted to `<strong>`, but `***bold***` would incorrectly wrap in `<strong>` twice).
3. **Performance**: For large inputs, consider optimizing with regex or a dedicated Markdown parser library (e.g., [Markdown-it](https://github.com/markdown-it/markdown-it)).

### Example Usage:
```cpp
#include <iostream>
int main() {
    std::string markdown = R"(
# Heading 1
**Bold** and *italic*
- List item 1
- List item 2
[Google](https://google.com)
---"
    );
    std::cout << markdownToHtml(markdown) << std::endl;
}
```
